Z||000000||Toogy||12-03-2001||11:43 AM||||What is the widest tire I get fit on the back of a 87 Fiero GT?  I am thinking maybe a 245/50R15 on the back and a 215/60R15 or 225/60R15 on the front.<BR>Will these stick out at all?  I don't want any tread sticking out.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR><B>Soon to be: 1987 GT 5-speed</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-03-2001||12:05 PM||||stock wheels? aftermarket wheels youll have to know what the offset is. I have 205/16/60 on front and had to grind a small bit on lower control arm. I have aftermarket wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Toogy||12-03-2001||12:24 PM||||They are aftermarket wheels, they are 15x7 I believe. I will be in-heriting this car from my Father-in-law.  The rims have been on the car for years and nobody has any idea what the offset is.  How can this be measured?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||fldevel||12-03-2001||12:39 PM||||i had 225s all the way around on my 85 GT so yes 225s will go up front no probs and the rims where stock too .. i dont think it would be any trouble to get 245s on the rear||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||12-03-2001||12:42 PM||||225/60-15 would be too tall on the front.  Go with a 225/50-15 instead.  It's close in height to the 245/50-15 if you run that on the back.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||12-03-2001||04:42 PM||||lay the wheel down flat with a straight edge across the top. then take a ruler or tape measure and measure the distance to the back of the center where lugs go from the straight edge. (thats the face that sits against the rotor when its mounted)||||reg||1
